How to Apply for an ADCB Credit Card?
The applicant can apply for ADCB Credit Card by visiting the nearest bank branch, submitting the credit card application online or via phone.
Nowadays, banks in the UAE offer an online application process. In order to understand the features, benefits, and requirement of the credit card, the applicants can click on the credit cards section on the official website of ADCB and opt for the credit card which suits their financial needs and requirements. They can click on the apply button, fill in the required information, and submit their credit card application. Once all the details are filled in, the bank officials will verify the credibility of the provided information. Based on the eligibility criteria of the applicant, they will decide whether the applicant will get the credit card or not.
Credit card experts recommend opting for a credit card on the basis of comparison. The applicant can compare various credit cards online.
The applicant can also apply for an ADCB credit card by visiting the nearest bank branch and apply for the credit card that suits their basic requirements. The applicant has to fill in all the basic details in the credit card application form. If they meet the eligibility criteria as per the bank’s guidelines, their credit card application will be taken forward.
The applicant can also apply for an ADCB credit card through the phone. All they’re required to is call the toll-free number on 600 56 2626.
The complete list of ADCB credit card charges can be found online.
How to Cancel an ADCB Credit Card?
In case the cardholder isn’t able to use the card, and they want to prevent charges from accumulating on the unused ADCB credit card, they should immediately cancel the card. It helps them to avoid paying extra charges.
For cancelling the ADCB credit card, cardholder needs to talk to ADCB representative and request for cancellation. The ADCB representative may require written confirmation for the same. Also, keep in mind that the cancel request will only be completed after all payment of the outstanding balance is made by the cardholder. Once all the dues have been paid, ADCB will cancel the credit card.
If the card member has been continuously missing paying their credit card bill.
If the card member uses the card for unlawful activities.
Why Choose ADCB’s Credit Card?
Ranging from free for life to high rewards credit cards; ADCB has managed to offer various categories for all types of credit card member. They can pick any of the credit cards that perfectly suit their need, lifestyle, and budget.
Another major reason for choosing ADCB credit cards is that they are loaded with exciting benefits and features which make shopping experience truly rewarding.
Majority of the credit cards have a tie-up with top brands such as VOX Cinemas, The Track Meydan Golf Dubai, Yas Links Golf Club Abu Dhabi, St. Regis Hotels & Resorts, Westin, W Hotels, and Sheraton and many which offer extra privileges and benefits to their cardholder.
Q.1. Can I make utility bill payments with my ADCB credit card?
Yes, you can make utility bill payments using your ADCB credit card.
Q.2. How many TouchPoints Credit Card does ADCB offer?
ADCB offers two TouchPoints Credit Cards- ADCB TouchPoints Infinite Credit Card with MyChoice and ADCB TouchPoints Credit Card with MyChoice which is available in 4 variants including Platinum, Titanium, Gold, and Classic credit cards.
Q.3. How can I use TouchPoints?
You earn TouchPoints every time when you use TouchPoints credit card. You can redeem the accumulated TouchPoints for booking airline tickets, shopping, dining, paying utility bills, fuel stations etc.
Q.4. What benefits are offered by LuLu Credit card?
LuLu Credit cards are specially designed for LuLu shoppers. You earn LuLu points every time you use this credit card. You can redeem the accumulated LuLu points for vouchers to spend at any of the LuLu stores in the UAE.
Every spend put on LuLu credit card earns points that can be redeemed for free shopping at a range of general stores including LuLu, AI Falah Plaza & Emirates general stores in the country.
Q.5. What are the variants available for the ADCB LuLu Credit card?
Currently, the ADCB LuLu Credit Card is available in the Titanium, Platinum, & Standard variants.
Q.6. Can supplementary card member avail complimentary airport lounge benefits?
Yes, supplementary card member can avail airport lounge benefits.
Q.7. Where I can use ADCB credit card?
You can use ADCB credit card anywhere in the world and can avail exclusive privileges each time you use the card.
Q.8. How can I update my mobile number?
You can update your mobile number by contacting customer care.
Q.9. Can I transfer my TouchPoints to someone’s account?
No, you can’t transfer your TouchPoints to someone’s account.
Q.10. What is an instalment plan?
An instalment plan allows the cardholder to pay for a big amount in smaller instalments over an agreed upon a number of months. In other words, the cardholder can purchase items within their credit card limit and pay the full amount over a period of time. Many banks offer zero interest instalment plan, which charges no additional amount for the monthly instalments. However, you should confirm whether the selected merchant is eligible for the instalment plan before making a purchase.
Well, ADCB offers zero interest instalment for its cardholder.

